# ---------- D2 Best rewrite (L4)
("D2",4,"Which is the best nominalised version of: \"Students who often put off their assignments until the last minute tend to perform worse on them\"?",
 ["Procrastination is associated with poorer academic performance.","Students who delay things do badly.","Don't leave your assignments until the last minute.","When students put things off, they will always fail."],
 "Nominalisation turns the long verb phrase 'put off assignments until the last minute' into the noun 'procrastination', making the sentence concise and academic."),
("D2",4,"Which is the most concise academic rewrite of: \"The thing that happens is that people who are lonely for a really long time end up feeling sad a lot\"?",
 ["Chronic loneliness may be associated with depressive symptoms.","Lonely people are sad.","People who are lonely for a long time will definitely become sad.","It seems like loneliness makes people feel really sad sometimes."],
 "It uses nouns (chronic loneliness, depressive symptoms), removes filler and keeps hedging ('may be associated')."),
("D2",4,"Which sentence has the HIGHEST lexical density?",
 ["Chronic stress impairs working-memory performance.","It is the case that stress can, in some ways, be bad for memory.","There are times when people who are stressed find it hard to remember things.","As we all know, stress is something that is not good for us."],
 "It packs the most content words (nouns, verbs, adjectives) into the fewest words, with almost no function words."),
("D2",4,"Which is the best rewrite of: \"In this essay I will be talking about the reasons why teenagers use their phones too much\"?",
 ["Excessive smartphone use among adolescents has several causes.","This essay will talk about phones.","I will now explain why teens use phones a lot.","Teenagers use phones way too much, which is bad."],
 "It removes telegraphing and personal pronouns and uses nominal style ('excessive smartphone use')."),
